{
  "pedal": "Boss RT-2 Rotary Ensemble, Modes I and II Drive, mono input A and stereo outputs A and B",
  "comment": "Mode III's Drive was measured with the rotors parked on 2026-11-21 (rt-2-focused.json); this is the same session for Mode I, then Mode II, one block of takes each. A block's first take checks the stored Balance and minimum Drive against the earlier two-rotor recording with the rotors turning; park the rotors after it and leave them parked to the block's end. At each setting the quiet sweep measures the response at that rotor angle. The 110 Hz and 441 Hz ladders measure the fundamental and its harmonics up to guitar level. The noise steps measure broadband compression and revisit the quiet level after the loudest step. The same ten seconds of funk follow each ladder. Compare horn, drum and both at minimum and 9 o’clock Drive. Leave the lead at noon out of the fit. The Drive/Balance entry shows which setting the outer ring controls. When resuming, set both stored values and finish with the toggle on the indicated side. A new stop can park the rotors at a different angle: a block resumed after its drive0700 takes starts again from its check. Each take's name carries the mode and the two stored values: horn = Balance 5:00, drum = Balance 7:00, both = Balance 12:00, then Drive's position.",
  "both_outputs": true,
  "marker_to_pedal": false,
  "quiet_dbfs": -60,
  "knobs": [
    "Mode",
    "Rise/Fall",
    "LED",
    "Level",
    "Drive/Balance",
    "Fast",
    "Slow"
  ],
